kage-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both public-task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence before and after restart. The mandatory restart protocol is also coherent: node1 was healthy on boot 368725cb-c64e-4393-b25f-da5111703b4a, acknowledged a scheduled reboot, returned on boot 95f60930-c5b8-41c9-b584-93f41caefda0, recovered its required services and policy, and passed another crash test. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently match that transition.","limitations":["Behavioral crash testing used one representative local service account, chrony UID 995; coverage of the remaining UID 1–999 accounts is supported by the observed range and system-wide policy rather than individual crash tests.","The standalone topology defines no separate application dataset or cluster service, so restart recovery evidence is limited to node health, required services, persisted policy, and post-restart crash behavior.","The trace cannot determine whether the failed transient-unit launch in cmd-6704f0ef5a9c4b66 briefly mutated runtime state; final observations show no associated failed-unit residue."]}
